#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:7
msgid ""
"This page describes how to configure health check probes for a Mattermost"
" server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:9
msgid ""
"Before you begin, you should have a running Mattermost server. If you "
"don't, you can :doc:`install Mattermost on various distributions "
"</deployment-guide/deployment-guide-index>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:13
msgid ""
":doc:`Highly available Mattermost cluster support </administration-"
"guide/scale/high-availability-cluster-based-deployment>` requires "
"Mattermost Enterprise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:15
msgid "You can perform a health check with the following 2 methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:17
msgid "`ping the APIv4 endpoint <#ping-the-apiv4-endpoint>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:18
msgid "`ping the Mattermost server <#ping-the-mattermost-server>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:21
msgid "Ping the APIv4 endpoint"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:23
#, python-format
msgid ""
"You can use the `GET /system/ping APIv4 endpoint "
"<https://api.mattermost.com/#tag/system%2Fpaths%2F~1system~1ping%2Fget>`_"
" to check for system health."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:25
msgid ""
"A sample request is included below. The endpoint checks if the server is "
"up and healthy based on the configuration setting "
"``GoRoutineHealthThreshold``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:27
msgid ""
"If ``GoRoutineHealthThreshold`` and the number of goroutines on the "
"server exceeds that threshold, the server is considered unhealthy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:28
msgid ""
"If ``GoRoutineHealthThreshold`` is not set or the number of goroutines is"
" below the threshold the server is considered healthy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:30
msgid ""
"This endpoint can also be provided to schedulers like `Kubernetes "
"<https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/configure-pod-container/configure-"
"liveness-readiness-startup-probes/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:43
msgid "Ping the Mattermost server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:45
msgid ""
"The `Mattermost Probe <https://github.com/csduarte/mattermost-probe>`_ "
"constantly pings a Mattermost server using a variety of probes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/manage/configure-health-check-probes.rst:47
msgid ""
"These probes can be configured to verify core features, including sending"
" and receiving messages, joining channels, pinging a login page, and "
"searching of users and channels."
msgstr ""

